WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.640
My right hand holds a bowl of gold,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.180
And my left holds one of silver.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.720
Never one without the other,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:37.800
Two unseen bowls for each of us.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:46.210
The golden one is filled with joy,

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:53.550
shining warmly.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.350
Since we met, my golden bowl

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:05.360
cannot hold all my happiness and love.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:15.500
Golden joy, silver sadness,

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:22.850
I would leave my past behind...

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:27.580
For you, for the sake of love,

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:34.520
I would empty the bowls of my past.

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:00.140
<i>Saint-Juste-sama...</i>

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:05.330
<i>Saint-Juste-sama, who was taken from us all too soon...</i>

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:09.780
<i>If she were still here with us now...</i>

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:14.330
<i>I'm sure that she would be laughing with joy. I'm sure of it.</i>

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:20.150
<i>I'm writing to tell you about something new and wonderful that has happened.</i>

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:26.600
<i>It happened on the final day of the week-long Port Festival...</i>

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:31.540
<i>Held each year to celebrate summer's end, it is the largest religious festival in these parts.</i>

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:35.960
<i>That day was the first time that I have gone with both my mother and my father.</i>

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:56.840
Ah! Papa, look! Over there!

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.110
Eh?

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.790
There, over by the second stone lantern.

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:01.390
Ah...

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:23.150
Allow me to introduce you. This is Orihara Kaoru-san.

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:25.420
She will be coming with me to Germany.

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:29.940
We're getting married.

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:34.010
Congratulations, Takehiko-san.

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:35.280
Thank you.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:48.360
<b>39. A Lingering Fragrance</b>

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:53.790
Finally, we're done with that horrid assignment!

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:57.340
Really, making us write a report on our impressions of Hemingway's works in English!

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:59.490
They can't do that to us, can they?! Sheesh...

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:01.160
Well, we managed somehow!

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:04.580
Yeah, we managed. I couldn't have done it without your help, though.

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.330
It was no trouble, really.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:12.350
Well, this is the right area, but where's this new place of Mariko's?

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:15.230
She said that there's supposed to be a kids' playground nearby.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:16.700
Hmm...

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.640
Ah! That's it right there!

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:23.610
Hey, that's a pretty nice-looking place, isn't it?

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:26.140
Welcome!

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:27.350
Ah! Welcome!

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:31.930
This place is really small compared to our old house, isn't it?

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:34.540
Mama and I share a bedroom, even.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.950
And the veranda... look at this, will you?

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:37.950
But it's OK, really.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:41.460
This is our castle.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.070
A castle for just the two of us, for Mama and me!

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:47.080
Come on, Mama! Bring out some of that Darjeeling tea!

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:50.430
Yes, yes, and some of the <i>creme brulee</i> cake, too, right?

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:53.880
Tea and cake are our only luxuries now.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.940
Wow, you can hear the steam whistles from here!

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:02.020
Yes. I don't know whether that's a good thing or not...

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:10.760
You know, I heard that Papa said that he'd like to see me each month.

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:14.950
I'm going to have to think on it a while.

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:18.430
After all, when it comes down to it, Papa was the one who betrayed us.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:23.400
My Papa had a son whom he didn't see for thirteen years...

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:31.040
And then that son decided to get married...

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:34.730
Papa saw then that his son had truly grown up.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:36.470
He looked happy.

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:40.890
Papa didn't say a word to us then, but he looked so very happy...

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:44.630
But still... you know what I thought?

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:49.340
As happy as Papa looked to be at the time...

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:54.430
...I'm sure that he was still feeling the sorrow and pain over all the time together that they never had.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:58.380
Nanako-san...

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:02.450
I... I've just been a bit out of it recently...

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:05.720
Nanako...

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:11.230
I know I'll never see Saint-Juste-sama again...

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:13.910
I've just felt kind of strange ever since then...

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:17.330
I've been concerning myself with other people's issues and ignoring my own.

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:22.150
None of that, now. I think the girl <i>still</i> hasn't gotten her emotions sorted out.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.900
No... no, I don't think that's it.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:28.520
I think that Nanako-san has simply grown up.

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:29.590
What?

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:32.670
You seem so much more mature that us now.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.160
You think so...?

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:37.970
We're the same age, you know...

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:41.390
Well, I'm not going to grow up.

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:44.600
I'm never going to understand other people's feelings!

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:47.280
Thinking of others just doesn't sit well with me.

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:52.140
So you really aren't going to go see your father?

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:55.360
I said I'd <i>think</i> about it, didn't I?!

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:57.970
Now, now, Mariko-san!

00:06:57.970 --> 00:07:01.860
What, like you're really the model of maturity yourself?!

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:04.800
Who, me? Heck, I could even be a mother by now, you know.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:05.810
Oh, come on!

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:09.900
What?! What's with you two?!

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:16.890
No, like I said, don't worry about that.

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:20.510
You should just be concentrating on getting ready for your studies in Germany.

00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:22.720
As for the reception hall, just leave it to me.

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:25.600
I may not look the social type, but I do know some people; we can get something set up for you.

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:31.160
Anyway, have you made the arrangements for her for while you're over there? Doctors, a school...?

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:32.830
Ah, OK.

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:34.310
Yeah... OK...

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:45.010
You called for me, Takashi-sama?

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:49.560
Yes. I'm sorry to trouble you, but could you prepare dinner a bit early tonight?

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:51.970
I have some things that I need to get back to work on this evening.

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:54.520
The preparations for the wedding ceremony?

00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:56.330
Yes, among other things.

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:58.740
You truly are a good friend to Henmi-sama.

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:00.420
He's heading off to Germany.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:03.770
I want to show him a good time while he's still here in Japan.

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:06.380
He must have found someone truly wonderful...

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:08.720
The very best.

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:11.740
Even better than Fukiko-sama...?

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:14.420
Igarashi...!

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:16.630
I'm sorry sir, that was very rude of me.

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:18.170
I am truly sorry.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:22.500
Well then... I shall start the dinner preparations at once.

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:26.840
Fukiko... where is she right now?

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:29.930
She left a while ago to go riding at the club, sir.

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:32.390
Ah, OK.

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:57.910
<i>In one summer, in one week...</i>

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:01.260
<i>...the love of a lifetime was forged...</i>

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:10.050
<i>Rei... Rei...!</i>

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:15.970
<i>In the end, you never did fall in love with a man...</i>

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:19.860
<i>If... if you had found someone to love...</i>

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:22.140
<i>...what would your love have been like, I wonder?</i>

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:25.550
<i>Unlike me, you were truly free.</i>

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:29.910
<i>You would be willing to devote yourself to someone, to give in to all your passions...</i>

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:32.990
<i>You would give your very life for it, I'm sure...</i>

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:43.530
<i>Painful though it may be, love is a truly wonderful thing.</i>

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:49.050
<i>Rei...</i>

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:53.720
<i>I really did want to see you fall in love.</i>

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:58.120
<i>I wanted to see you even more radiant than ever before...</i>

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:00.460
<i>I only regret that I never saw it...</i>

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:06.480
<i>Shall I compare thee to a summer's day?</i>

00:10:06.490 --> 00:10:11.980
<i>Thou art more lovely and more temperate...</i>

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:15.150
<i>Fukiko-sama?</i>

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:17.820
<i>Fukiko-sama...</i>

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:22.440
<i>Is that your love?</i>

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:24.780
<i>Is that all that there is to your love?</i>

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:27.730
<i>One summer, one week, and then nothing more?</i>

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:29.900
Yes.

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:32.870
<i>That wasn't love.</i>

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:34.280
It was love!

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:36.830
That was my one love in this life.

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:38.700
<i>You are like I was...</i>

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:41.450
<i>You have not yet known true love.</i>

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:43.190
I did!

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:48.680
<i>A toast to you - may you find love anew!</i>

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:50.970
It is not possible.

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:56.650
I could never...

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:01.140
A new love...? Never!

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:04.520
That was it, that was the real thing!

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:07.940
My one and only love...

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:10.550
I shall never love another.

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:12.030
I swore, upon my very life...

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:27.220
Fukiko!

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:30.230
It was getting so late, I was worried that you might have fallen or something...

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:35.460
Fukiko...!

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:39.180
I see...

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:42.060
Were you thinking about Rei again?

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:46.210
No... No, that wasn't it at all...

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:58.830
<i>Rei... is this what you wanted?</i>

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:20.780
The new semester is finally here, isn't it.

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:22.060
Yes.

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:26.280
You've been through some pretty difficult ordeals this summer, but...

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:28.350
...you've managed to sort out your feelings over it all, right?

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:29.220
Yes.

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:32.920
And how about physically?

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:34.870
Are you ready?

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:37.010
Sure! Everything's OK!

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:42.720
Well, then... what's on your mind? You were the one who invited me out this morning.

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:49.420
The new semester is starting, and you invited me out here, as though you wanted to ask me something again.

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:51.160
So... what is it?

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:52.570
Hmm...

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:56.910
I can't help but be a bit anxious, wondering what sort of question you'll spring on me this time.

00:12:57.530 --> 00:12:58.740
Oh goodness, Papa...

00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:01.620
How am I supposed to ask you something when you're already jumping ahead like that...

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:04.440
It's something you feel nervous about asking, I take it?

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:05.710
Yeah...

00:13:05.710 --> 00:13:07.920
Now I really <i>am</i> getting nervous...

00:13:11.590 --> 00:13:14.870
Don't worry. Whatever it is, I'll give you a straight answer.

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:16.010
OK.

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:27.130
I've been wanting to ask you, Papa. I wanted to ask you first, before asking Mama.

00:13:27.130 --> 00:13:30.150
For a while now... for quite a while, really...

00:13:30.150 --> 00:13:31.220
OK.

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:34.700
I'm not your real daughter, Papa...

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:41.750
I want to know about my real father. I want to know everything!

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:46.880
Now, you love me, Papa...

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:48.950
...and I love you, too.

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:51.500
I want you to understand how important that is to me.

00:13:55.560 --> 00:14:00.520
Really, I think that we could still be just as happy even if we never discussed this...

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:07.220
...but I would hate to think that something truly important to me might one day be lost forever.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:15.880
Please, Papa! Tell me anything that you know!

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:20.040
Who is my father? Where is he now? What kind of person is he?

00:14:22.350 --> 00:14:26.780
Your Mama never did marry him.

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:30.190
Apparently, she did live with him for a long time...

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:34.550
...but once you were conceived, and before you were born, she left him.

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:39.040
That's all I know... No, it is all speculation, really...

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:48.490
I have never once asked your Mam about any of that.

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:50.640
You understand why, don't you?

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:54.050
Even if I were to ask her, she is not the sort of person who would ever want to talk about it.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:01.950
For my sake, or for yours... perhaps for both of us, really...

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:05.240
...I think that Mama has chosen to keep those things locked away forever.

00:15:08.290 --> 00:15:11.770
Even so, I love her dearly.

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:14.380
She is beautiful in my eyes.

00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:16.120
There's nothing wrong with that, is there?

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:20.490
For your Papa here, things are fine as they are.

00:15:20.490 --> 00:15:23.970
But I am who I am; you are your own person, Nanako.

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:29.530
If the time comes someday when you feel that you truly must know...

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:31.680
...then don't hesitate on my account.

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:34.420
Go ahead and ask Mama if she will unlock those secrets within her heart.

00:15:34.420 --> 00:15:38.040
But... that's why I came to you, Papa...

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:43.650
Because even you know that Mama is not the sort who would ever tell.

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:44.730
I understand.

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:56.380
Even you, Nanako, must have one or two secrets that you will keep locked away forever.

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:05.650
Even knowing that, you can still love and believe in someone, right?

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:13.850
Well anyway... we're going to be late for breakfast.

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:19.870
Everything's OK?

00:16:22.390 --> 00:16:24.400
Sure! It's OK!

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:34.540
<i>And so began the new term.</i>

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:36.900
Good morning, Nanako-san!

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:43.610
<i>Mariko-san's suspension was reduced, too, so she was able to start the new semester with us.</i>

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:50.720
<i>Misaki-san, Sonobe-san, Furuta-san...</i>

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:54.940
<i>...all of those who had been Sorority members before it was abolished...</i>

00:16:54.940 --> 00:16:58.160
<i>...and of course, Miya-sama as well...</i>

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:05.610
<i>Those bright summer days were coming to an end.</i>

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:08.560
<i>So many things had happend that summer; but it was over now.</i>

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:11.040
<i>Each of us had overcome something.</i>

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:17.070
<i>You could see it in our faces... cheerful, confident, perhaps a bit more mature.</i>

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:27.780
<i>Only one person was with us no more. Like the wind, she bade us farewell, and left forever.</i>

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:34.600
<i>She will forever shine brightly in our hearts, one page in the story of our youth.</i>

00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:37.350
<i>And so, the seasons changed...</i>

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:55.980
<i>My dear brother...</i>

00:17:55.980 --> 00:17:59.190
<i>I watched Kaoru-no-Kimi's game.</i>

00:17:59.860 --> 00:18:02.610
<i>It was the final match of the area league championships.</i>

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:06.830
<i>It was the final game for Seiran Academy's ace, Kaoru-no-Kimi.</i>

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:14.240
<i>Kaoru-no-Kimi wore the number "16" in that game.</i>

00:18:14.790 --> 00:18:18.340
<i>That number once belonged to her - to Saint-Juste-sama.</i>

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:24.320
<i>No doubt, Kaoru-no-Kimi fought that final match with that person at her side.</i>

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:30.060
<i>Clearly the other students from Seiran Academy noticed it as well.</i>

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:37.760
<i>Everyone was applauding and cheering just as loudly as they could as they watched the game.</i>

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:51.030
<i>And then, my brother...</i>

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:56.710
<i>Then came the most important day of all, for both you and Kaoru-no-Kimi.</i>

00:18:56.710 --> 00:18:58.780
<i>It was raining that day, too...</i>

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:00.990
Henmi Takehiko...

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:05.220
...do you promise to love this woman, Orihara Kaoru, as your wife...

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:09.300
...through times of sickness, through times of health, for all time, until death do you part?

00:19:09.300 --> 00:19:11.180
I do.

00:19:13.030 --> 00:19:15.040
Orihara Kaoru...

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:19.600
...do you promise to love this man, Henmi Takehiko, as your husband...

00:19:19.600 --> 00:19:23.490
...through times of sickness, through times of health, for all time, until death do you part?

00:19:23.490 --> 00:19:25.090
I do.

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:29.380
For so long as I shall live...

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:44.610
<i>My dear brother...</i>

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:50.040
<i>...that eighteen-year-old bride shone more brightly that day than anything in the world.</i>

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:55.180
<i>Her lips, painted a delicate rose, and her cheeks, touched with blush...</i>

00:19:55.180 --> 00:20:00.540
<i>She was truly full of life that day, living for the sake of love, shining for all to see.</i>

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:03.250
<i>"For so long as I shall live..."</i>

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:08.400
<i>Those words filled her heart as she spoke them for the one she loved.</i>

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:11.550
<i>Someday, I, too, will be able to say such a thing...</i>

00:20:11.550 --> 00:20:14.700
<i>That's what I was thinking that day.</i>

00:20:15.820 --> 00:20:19.230
<i>I will one day be able to say such words as those.</i>

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:24.700
<i>I hope to someday find such a love, that I can say such words as those...</i>

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:26.500
<i>I wish it with all my heart...</i>

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:46.050
This is wonderful, isn't it, Kaoru-no-Kimi?

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:48.600
All the romantic country roads, and then there's the Rhine river...

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:51.410
Oh, oh, and the sausage there is supposed to be really good, too!

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:52.550
Yeah.

00:20:52.550 --> 00:20:56.510
If we get the chance, we're going to tour some of the old castles, too.

00:20:56.510 --> 00:20:57.910
That's so wonderful!

00:20:57.910 --> 00:21:00.190
Splendid... just splendid...

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:01.660
Just... splendid...

00:21:02.140 --> 00:21:03.690
Mariko-san...

00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:07.740
Be happy, Kaoru-no-Kimi...

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:09.410
Really, I mean it...

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:13.360
Come on, Henmi. It's about time.

00:21:13.360 --> 00:21:14.900
Oh, yeah...

00:21:19.450 --> 00:21:21.190
I'm going now, Father.

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:26.960
Be well... Mother...

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:33.090
Thank you, Takehiko-san. You take care, too.

00:21:37.510 --> 00:21:38.650
Later!

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:41.980
My brother...

00:21:44.140 --> 00:21:45.680
I'll write to you!

00:21:51.810 --> 00:21:54.290
Take care of Kaoru-no-Kimi!

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:00.860
<i>For just a moment...</i>

00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:04.410
<i>For just a moment, as I stood there beside my brother...</i>

00:22:04.410 --> 00:22:09.630
<i>...I caught the nostalgic scent of that one person who will never again return.</i>

00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:12.600
<i>That scent, Saint-Juste-sama's fragrance...</i>

00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:15.080
<i>That subtle, masculine air...</i>

00:22:18.130 --> 00:22:23.550
<i>Perhaps it was the scent of tobacco that so often surrounded her.</i>

00:22:24.830 --> 00:22:31.130
<i>The plane carried away not only my brother and Kaoru-no-Kimi, but also that nostalgic lingering fragrance...</i>

00:22:32.020 --> 00:22:33.020
Nanako!

00:22:33.020 --> 00:22:33.890
Nanako-san!

00:22:52.260 --> 00:22:55.000
<i>Since then, the cherry blossoms have bloomed twice.</i>

00:22:55.600 --> 00:22:58.690
<i>I'm a senior at Seiran Academy now.</i>

00:22:59.380 --> 00:23:02.060
<i>I just received the wonderful news from Germany...</i>

00:23:13.340 --> 00:23:16.550
<i>My dear brother, I have something wonderful to tell you, myself.</i>

00:23:17.720 --> 00:23:22.010
<i>Recently, I have met someone whom I've taken a bit of a liking to.</i>

00:23:23.300 --> 00:23:26.190
<i>He's a second-year student at the University...</i>

00:23:28.620 --> 00:23:33.780
<i>...although... he doesn't have dark-brown eyes...</i>

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:14.360
I dreamed I was chasing a rainbow...

00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:19.830
Then the rainbow I was chasing was you.

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:25.440
Before, I had no strength, no will.

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:30.910
But now because of you, I do.

00:24:31.650 --> 00:24:37.190
Feelings of love, like raindrops

00:24:37.190 --> 00:24:42.660
Come pouring from the sky.

00:24:42.660 --> 00:24:45.390
This is surely a game

00:24:45.390 --> 00:24:48.200
Of some mischievous fairy...

00:24:48.200 --> 00:24:50.600
Always dancing,

00:24:50.600 --> 00:24:55.870
Always capricious...
